SOAPBOX: It is a pity that no distinction is made in the antenna
SOAPBOX: configurations.
SOAPBOX: I work with a wire and a vertical antenna. So,
SOAPBOX: there is a bit of a disadvantage with the beams on the higher
SOAPBOX: bands.
SOAPBOX: Also, the RTTY signal is rarely listened to. It is
SOAPBOX: also unfortunate regarding some high-power stations near weak or
SOAPBOX: special stations. The rare station sends a callsign with RPT, but
SOAPBOX: because it is a rare station, they just keep sending their
SOAPBOX: callsign and no longer listen to what the rare station is
SOAPBOX: transmitting.
SOAPBOX: In this way, a lot of time is lost because the
SOAPBOX: rare station still tries to work its opposing station.
SOAPBOX: Work with Yaesu FTdx101D (70w) and ant Skyloop(HM) + R8 (vert)
